# Build context exclusions for infra/docker/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's `.dockerignore`, which
# is what makes this file effective without touching the repository root — that file belongs to another
# stream.
#
# Excluding node_modules matters more than it looks: pnpm's store holds platform-specific binaries, and
# shipping a Windows Prisma engine into an Alpine image is a confusing failure. The build installs its
# own from the committed lockfile.

.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
.next
**/.next
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo

# Local database and generated Prisma artefacts. `pnpm --filter @grihaone/db generate` recreates the
# schemas and clients inside the image.
.data
packages/db/prisma/generated
packages/db/prisma/*/schema.prisma

# Nothing in the image reads these.
docs
.obsidian
coverage
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
*.log

# Terraform state and provider binaries are large and have no business in a container.
infra/**/.terraform
infra/**/*.tfstate
infra/**/*.tfstate.*
infra/**/*.tfvars

# Secrets, in case one exists locally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
